ow most  of those who aren't currently vaccinated  they're not necessarily anti-vaxxers but  they've not yet been determined enough  to go and get a vaccine because they  could have done  it okay but he seems to be suggesting  that the shooter was waiting to get  vaccinated  before doing the mass shooting the  shooter appears to have planned to die  yesterday  if you plan to either shoot yourself or  get police to shoot you  after shooting up your workplace why are  you waiting for the vaccine  maybe you want for your workers to be  co-workers to be back at work so that  you can have a bunch of them together to  shoot okay yeah that may be something  you're waiting for  but what a completely hair brained idea  and this is by far the stupidest way  i've seen to criticize vaccines  uh from from the entirety of this  pandemic if there has ever been a  cautionary tale  about understanding the difference  between correlation and causation  it's looking at an example like this  mass shooters  are not notoriously fastidious about  being vaccinated before going out and  doing a mass shooting  it there's just we that that's not the  case and then it's also important to  mention  implicit in his argument is that  coronavirus shutdowns  are good in terms of they limit mass  shootings  my guess is this is not a guy who is too  thrilled with coronavirus guidelines  just from how he talks dismissively  about vaccination  but what he seems to be saying is when  we were quote  locked down which we never were it  actually did work to decrease mass  shootings which is an interesting thing  to hear from a guy  who is making no sense about any of his  arguments disgusting  sick argument to be making if you ever  feel  like you just don't have enough time to  read all the books you want  to read you have to check out one of my  favorite apps  called blinkist blinkist takes thousands  of popular nonfiction books  and distills each one down into an  e-book or audiobook  that you can get t